<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Notation and omitted details</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we include some technical details concerning the theoretical results of the paper that were omitted for the sake of readability.</p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Properties of the forward process</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#S1" title="1 Introduction: Diffusion, manifolds and generalisation ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, we introduced the forward process in (<a href="#S1.E1" title="Equation 1 ‣ 1 Introduction: Diffusion, manifolds and generalisation ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). Throughout the proofs, we use the following property of the forward process:</p>
<table id="A1.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="X_{t}|X_{0}\sim N(\mu_{t}X_{0},\sigma_{t}I_{d}),\qquad\mu_{t}=e^{-\alpha t},\qquad\sigma^{2}_{t}=\begin{cases}\alpha^{-1}(1-\mu_{t}^{2}),&amp;\text{if }\alpha&gt;0,\\
2t,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext>otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}|X_{0}\sim N(\mu_{t}X_{0},\sigma_{t}I_{d}),\qquad\mu_{t}=e^{-\alpha t},\qquad\sigma^{2}_{t}=\begin{cases}\alpha^{-1}(1-\mu_{t}^{2}),&amp;\text{if }\alpha&gt;0,\\
2t,&amp;\text{otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>, this follows immediately from properties of the Wiener process and when <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> becomes the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process and the result follows from a standard analysis (e.g. see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pavliotis [2014]</a></cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Using this fact, we have the following closed-form expression for the density <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, the density of the empirical forward process <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{X}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>X</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{X}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\bigg(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{X_{t}|X_{0}}(x|x_{i})\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\bigg(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}p_{X_{t}|X_{0}}(x|x_{i})\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\log\bigg(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(-\|x-\mu_{t}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})\bigg)-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\log\bigg(\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(-\|x-\mu_{t}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})\bigg)-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\|x-\mu_{t}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg)+C_{t}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>LSE</mi><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\|x-\mu_{t}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{t}^{2})\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg)+C_{t},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}=-\log(N)-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}=-\log(N)-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{t}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and we recall the definition of the function <math id="A1.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LSE}(\{r_{i}\}_{i}):=\log(\sum_{i}\exp(r_{i}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LSE}(\{r_{i}\}_{i}):=\log(\sum_{i}\exp(r_{i}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Rényi divergence</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We provide a brief exposition of the Rényi divergence, which is a measure of difference between two measures. Given two measures <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\nu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\nu</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in(1,\infty)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in(1,\infty)</annotation></semantics></math> we define the <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>-Rényi divergence by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int(\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}(x))^{q-1}\mu(dx),&amp;\text{ if }\mu\ll\nu,\\
\infty,&amp;\text{ otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext> otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)=\begin{cases}\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int(\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}(x))^{q-1}\mu(dx),&amp;\text{ if }\mu\ll\nu,\\
\infty,&amp;\text{ otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For the case of <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=1</annotation></semantics></math> we set <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the Kullback-Leibler (KL) divergence,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{1}(\mu\|\nu)=\begin{cases}\int\log\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}(x)\ \mu(dx),&amp;\text{ if }\mu\ll\nu,\\
\infty,&amp;\text{ otherwise.}\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext> if </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mo>≪</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mtext> otherwise.</mtext></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}(\mu\|\nu)=\begin{cases}\int\log\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}(x)\ \mu(dx),&amp;\text{ if }\mu\ll\nu,\\
\infty,&amp;\text{ otherwise.}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">Indeed, whenever <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, it can be shown that <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim_{q\to 1^{+}}D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)=D_{1}(\mu\|\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{q\to 1^{+}}D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)=D_{1}(\mu\|\nu)</annotation></semantics></math>. Furthermore, whenever <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>-almost surely, we obtain,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lim_{q\to\infty}D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)=\log\bigg(\operatorname{ess\,sup}_{\mu}\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}\bigg)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mi>ess</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>sup</mi></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>μ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{q\to\infty}D_{q}(\mu\|\nu)=\log\bigg(\operatorname{ess\,sup}_{\mu}\frac{d\mu}{d\nu}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">which is taken to be <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\infty}(\mu\|\nu)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ν</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\infty}(\mu\|\nu)</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, the Rényi divergence provides a natural interpolation between the KL divergence and the worst-case regret, with <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> increasing in <math id="A1.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>. This measure of distance recently gained popularity in the sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Vempala and Wibisono, 2019</a>, <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chewi et al., 2022</a>, <a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Erdogdu et al., 2022</a>, <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mousavi-Hosseini et al., 2023</a>]</cite> and privacy <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mironov, 2017</a>]</cite> literatures as a stronger alternative to traditional divergences. We refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">van Erven and Harremoes, 2014</a>]</cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chewi et al., 2022</a>]</cite> for further properties of this divergence.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Projections</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout this work, we frequently utilise the projection mapping <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}:\mathbb{R}^{d}\to{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> which maps <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> to the nearest element of <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. In cases where <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is curved, we run in to the issue that the projection is not well-defined as there could be multiple elements that are equally close to <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. In most places in the proof we consider quantities <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> that are sufficiently close that the projection function is uniquely defined (see reach in Appendix <a href="#A3.SS2" title="C.2 Manifold reach ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>) but, for example, when we define the manifold adapted kernel in (<a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>), we use the projection for all <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Throughout the proofs of this work we do not utilise any property of the projection aside from the fact that it maps <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> to some element of the manifold that is of distance <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> away from <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. For that reason, <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> can be taken to be any mapping onto <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x)\|=\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x)\|=\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A1.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> is taken to be a closed set, such a mapping always exists and we will take this choice of mapping to be fixed throughout the work.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> the samples generated at early stopping time <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> are slightly biased due to contractions of the Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process. For this reason, we will frequently consider the contracted manifold,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\epsilon}{\mathcal{M}}=\{\mu_{\epsilon}x:x\in{\mathcal{M}}\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\epsilon}{\mathcal{M}}=\{\mu_{\epsilon}x:x\in{\mathcal{M}}\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is as defined in (<a href="#A1.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ A.1 Properties of the forward process ‣ Appendix A Notation and omitted details ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>), and we will frequently use the shorthand <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}:=\mu_{\epsilon}{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}:=\mu_{\epsilon}{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Given a projection mapping <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we take the projection mapping <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A1.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> to be given by</p>
<table id="A1.Ex18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)=\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x/\mu_{\epsilon})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)=\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x/\mu_{\epsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Manifold-adaptivity in the affine setting</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> concerning the affine setting. Recall that we assume that the support of <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\operatorname{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\operatorname{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> is restricted to the affine subspace <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:Ax=b\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:Ax=b\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{*}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{*}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> is row-orthonormal and <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>b</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b\in\mathbb{R}^{d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we write the smoothing kernel in the following form:</p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{x}:=\operatorname{law}(x+\xi)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>law</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{x}:=\operatorname{law}(x+\xi),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ξ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi</annotation></semantics></math> is a centred random variable independent of <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Throughout the proof, we will use the null space projection matrix <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P:=I-A^{T}A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P:=I-A^{T}A</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem1" title="Proposition 3.1. ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is the projection matrix onto <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Null}(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Null</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Null}(A)</annotation></semantics></math>, any <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> can be decomposed as</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|z\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|z\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|Pz\|^{2}+\|(I-P)z\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|Pz\|^{2}+\|(I-P)z\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|Pz\|^{2}+\|A^{T}Az\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|Pz\|^{2}+\|A^{T}Az\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|Pz\|^{2}+\|Az\|^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|Pz\|^{2}+\|Az\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the final line follows from the fact that <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is row-orthonormal and so <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AA^{T}=I_{d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mi>T</mi></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AA^{T}=I_{d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fact</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and the assumption that <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Ax_{i}=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Ax_{i}=b</annotation></semantics></math> for every <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the identity</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|z-x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)+C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|z-x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)+C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(z-x_{i})\|^{2}+\|A(z-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)+C_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(z-x_{i})\|^{2}+\|A(z-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)+C_{t}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(z-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)-\frac{\|Az-b\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+C_{t}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>z</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(z-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)-\frac{\|Az-b\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+C_{t}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">This decomposition separates the influence of <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math> into normal and tangent directions with respect to <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Now, let <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{x}=(x+\xi)\sim k_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{x}=(x+\xi)\sim k_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widetilde{Y}_{x}=(x+P\xi)\sim k_{x}^{{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widetilde{Y}_{x}=(x+P\xi)\sim k_{x}^{{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P=P^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P=P^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we observe that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|P(Y_{x}-x_{i})\|=\|P(\tilde{Y}_{x}-x_{i})\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|P(Y_{x}-x_{i})\|=\|P(\tilde{Y}_{x}-x_{i})\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Furthermore, using the fact that <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ξ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> is centred, we also have,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\|AY_{x}-b\|^{2}]=\|Ax-b\|^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\|A\xi\|^{2}],\qquad\mathbb{E}[\|A\tilde{Y}_{x}-b\|^{2}]=\|Ax-b\|^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\|AP\xi\|^{2}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\|AY_{x}-b\|^{2}]=\|Ax-b\|^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\|A\xi\|^{2}],\qquad\mathbb{E}[\|A\tilde{Y}_{x}-b\|^{2}]=\|Ax-b\|^{2}+\mathbb{E}[\|AP\xi\|^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">In particular, substituting into (<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation 16 ‣ Proof of Proposition . ‣ Appendix B Manifold-adaptivity in the affine setting ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) and taking the expectation, we conclude that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(Y_{x})]=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(Y_{x}-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)\bigg]-\frac{\|Ax-b\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+C," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(Y_{x})]=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(Y_{x}-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)\bigg]-\frac{\|Ax-b\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+C,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(\tilde{Y}_{x})]=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(Y_{x}-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)\bigg]-\frac{\|Ax-b\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\tilde{C}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(\tilde{Y}_{x})]=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|P(Y_{x}-x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)\bigg]-\frac{\|Ax-b\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\tilde{C},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">for constants <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C,\tilde{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C,\tilde{C}</annotation></semantics></math> independent of <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the log-density of <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> are identical up to a constant.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Lemmata</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For proving the results for the more the general manifold setting, we require several additional properties of the log-sum-exp function, smooth manifolds and tubular neighbourhoods. In this section we collect these results.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Stability of the <math id="A3.SS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LSE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LSE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LSE}</annotation></semantics></math> function</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma provides stability bounds for the LSE function which we make use of throughout our analysis. It can be seen as a generalisation of Fact <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> which is heavily used in the analysis of the affine case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\varepsilon_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\varepsilon_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N}\subset\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+\epsilon_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})-\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})}dr." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+\epsilon_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})-\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})=\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})}dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+\epsilon_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})-\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})\leq\max\{\epsilon_{i}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+\epsilon_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})-\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N})\leq\max\{\epsilon_{i}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the chain rule, we compute the partial derivatives,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i})=\frac{\exp(x_{j})}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i})=\frac{\exp(x_{j})}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, by the fundamental theorem of calculus, we obtain that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+\epsilon_{i}\}_{i})-\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+\epsilon_{i}\}_{i})-\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}\}_{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\epsilon_{j}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i}\}_{i})\,dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\epsilon_{j}\frac{\partial}{\partial x_{j}}\operatorname{LSE}(\{x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i}\}_{i})\,dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\frac{\exp(x_{j}+r\epsilon_{j})\epsilon_{j}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})}dr," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{1}\sum_{j=1}^{N}\frac{\exp(x_{j}+r\epsilon_{j})\epsilon_{j}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})}dr,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">completing the proof of (<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Stability of the LSE function ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). To obtain (<a href="#A3.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Stability of the LSE function ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>), we use the fact that the sum is a weighted average of the sequence <math id="A3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\epsilon_{i}\}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\epsilon_{i}\}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and so it has the property that,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(x_{j}+r\epsilon_{j})}\leq\max_{i}\epsilon_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{\exp(x_{i}+r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}\exp(x_{j}+r\epsilon_{j})}\leq\max_{i}\epsilon_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS1.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS1.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We also note that if all <math id="A3.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> are identical, we readily recover Fact <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> from (<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Stability of the LSE function ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Manifold reach</h3>

<div id="A3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Next, we collect some facts about the <span id="A3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">reach</span> of the manifold, which quantifies how far one can extend from the manifold before the projection onto it ceases to be unique. We refer to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aamari, 2017</a>]</cite> for a more detailed exposition. We begin with the rigorous definition.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The reach of a set <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subset\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, is defined by <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{A}=\inf_{p\in A}d(p,Med(A))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{A}=\inf_{p\in A}d(p,Med(A))</annotation></semantics></math>, where we define the set,</p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="Med(A)=\Big\{z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\exists p,q\in A\text{ s.t. }p\neq q,\|p-z\|=\|q-z\|=d(z,A)\Big\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mi>e</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∃</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi><mtext> s.t. </mtext><mi>p</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">=</mo><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Med(A)=\Big\{z\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\exists p,q\in A\text{ s.t. }p\neq q,\|p-z\|=\|q-z\|=d(z,A)\Big\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The reach defines the maximum distance at which the projection to the set is unique. In the case where the set <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is a smooth submanifold of <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, the reach captures the curvature of the manifold and provides an upper bound on the distance at which the manifold appears approximately flat. The following lemma demonstrates this, controlling the curvature of paths along the manifold using the reach. We use the notation <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> to denote the <span id="A3.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">normal space</span> of the manifold <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> which consists of all vectors perpendicular to the tangent space at <math id="A3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.3</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the manifold <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> has reach <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\langle v,x-y\rangle|\leq\frac{\|v\|}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|x-y\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\langle v,x-y\rangle|\leq\frac{\|v\|}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|x-y\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> and define <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z=x+rv/\|v\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z=x+rv/\|v\|</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\not\in Med({\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∉</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\not\in Med({\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the projection is uniquely defined with <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(z)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(z)=x</annotation></semantics></math>, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|z-y\|\geq\operatorname{dist}(z,M)=r." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|z-y\|\geq\operatorname{dist}(z,M)=r.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|z-y\|^{2}=\|x-y\|^{2}+r^{2}+\frac{2r}{\|v\|}\langle x-y,v\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|z-y\|^{2}=\|x-y\|^{2}+r^{2}+\frac{2r}{\|v\|}\langle x-y,v\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these two and rearranging, we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle y-x,v\rangle\leq\frac{\|v\|}{2r}\|x-y\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle y-x,v\rangle\leq\frac{\|v\|}{2r}\|x-y\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">By replacing <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-v</annotation></semantics></math> which is also in the normal space, we obtain the opposite direction, hence obtaining,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\langle x-y,v\rangle|\leq\frac{\|v\|}{2r}\|x-y\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\langle x-y,v\rangle|\leq\frac{\|v\|}{2r}\|x-y\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since this bound holds for all <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we can take <math id="A3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\to\tau_{\mathcal{M}}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\to\tau_{\mathcal{M}}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the bound in the statement.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With this, we can control the geodesic distance on the manifold by the standard Euclidean distance.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.4</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the manifold <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> has reach <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|x-y\|\leq\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|x-y\|\leq\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be a geodesic (shortest path) between <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A3.Thmtheorem4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we have the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt\leq 2\|x-y\|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt\leq 2\|x-y\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Therefore, if we are close enough to the manifold, its inherited metric behaves roughly like the Euclidean one. The proof of this lemma can be found in Lemma III.21 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aamari, 2017</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.3 </span>Concentration under the manifold hypothesis</h3>

<div id="A3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn to results concerning probability measures supported on submanifolds with bounded reach. The next lemma controls the mass of a small ball centred on the manifold, showing that the rates are similar to the affine case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.5</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the measure <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\operatorname{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\operatorname{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> is supported on a smooth compact submanifold <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> with reach <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and dimension <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq\pi\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2\sqrt{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq\pi\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2\sqrt{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{r}(x))\geq c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}},\qquad c_{\mu}=\inf_{B_{r}(x)}p_{\mu}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{r}(x))\geq c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}},\qquad c_{\mu}=\inf_{B_{r}(x)}p_{\mu},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the density of <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\operatorname{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\operatorname{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to the volume measure on <math id="A3.Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For the proof of this lemma, we refer to the proof of Proposition 4.3 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aamari et al., 2019</a>]</cite> or Lemma III.23 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aamari, 2017</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">We use this bound, to obtain a result concerning the concentration of the empirical measure on the manifold. To this end, we recall a bound on the covering number of the manifold. Given <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, the covering number <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{cov}}({\mathcal{M}},r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext>cov</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{cov}}({\mathcal{M}},r)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as the minimum number of Euclidean balls of radius <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> required to cover the subset of <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> defined by the space <math id="A3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The following lemma is from Proposition III.11 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Aamari [2017]</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.6</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the setting of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma C.5. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> and suppose that <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mu}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mu}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2)</annotation></semantics></math> we have,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\text{cov}}({\mathcal{M}},2\varepsilon)\leq\frac{1}{c_{\mu}\varepsilon^{d^{*}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">cov</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\text{cov}}({\mathcal{M}},2\varepsilon)\leq\frac{1}{c_{\mu}\varepsilon^{d^{*}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">We can now prove a bound on the concentration of the empirical measure.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.7</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that the measure <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\operatorname{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\operatorname{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> is supported on a compact smooth submanifold <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> with reach <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and dimension <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mu}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mu}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex40" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\bigg(\inf_{x\in M}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{r}(x))\geq c_{\mu}\frac{r^{d^{*}}}{4}\bigg)\geq 1-\delta," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\bigg(\inf_{x\in M}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{r}(x))\geq c_{\mu}\frac{r^{d^{*}}}{4}\bigg)\geq 1-\delta,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">whenever,</span></p>
<table id="A3.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 64\Big((144d^{*}\log(2/r)+144\log(2/c_{\mu}))\vee\tfrac{\log(\delta^{-1})}{2}\Big)r^{-2d^{*}}c_{\mu}^{-2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>144</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>144</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 64\Big((144d^{*}\log(2/r)+144\log(2/c_{\mu}))\vee\tfrac{\log(\delta^{-1})}{2}\Big)r^{-2d^{*}}c_{\mu}^{-2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma C.6. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.6</span></a>, there exists a set <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}\subset{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}\subset{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\{B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c):c\in\mathcal{C}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c):c\in\mathcal{C}\}</annotation></semantics></math> forms a covering of <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{C}|\leq c_{\mu}^{-1}2^{d^{*}+1}r^{-d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{C}|\leq c_{\mu}^{-1}2^{d^{*}+1}r^{-d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, for any <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in M</annotation></semantics></math> there exists <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c\in\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c\in\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="x\in B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c)</annotation></semantics></math> and therefore <math id="A3.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c)\subset B_{r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c)\subset B_{r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>. From this we deduce the following bound</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex41" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\inf_{x\in{\mathcal{M}}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{r}(x))\geq\inf_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{x\in{\mathcal{M}}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{r}(x))\geq\inf_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, it suffices to lower bound this object on the right-hand side.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, using a rudimentary bound from the empirical processes literature (for example, see Section 4.2 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright, 2019</a>]</cite> or Section 7.1 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib69" title="" class="ltx_ref">van Handel, 2014</a>]</cite>), we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{P}\bigg(\sup_{c\in\mathcal{C}}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))|\geq 12\sqrt{\frac{\log{|\mathcal{C}|}}{N}}+\varepsilon\bigg)\leq\exp(-2N\varepsilon^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><mn>12</mn><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>N</mi></mfrac></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\bigg(\sup_{c\in\mathcal{C}}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))|\geq 12\sqrt{\frac{\log{|\mathcal{C}|}}{N}}+\varepsilon\bigg)\leq\exp(-2N\varepsilon^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, choosing <math id="A3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}}/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}}/8</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that under (<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>), it follows that</span></p>
<table id="A3.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\bigg(\sup_{C\in\mathcal{C}}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(C)-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(C)|\geq c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}}/4\bigg)\leq\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\bigg(\sup_{C\in\mathcal{C}}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(C)-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(C)|\geq c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}}/4\bigg)\leq\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">To conclude the proof, we use Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem5" title="Lemma C.5. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.5</span></a> to obtain that,</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\inf_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\inf_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex43.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\inf_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))-\sup_{c\in M}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\inf_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))-\sup_{c\in M}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(c))|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}}/2-\sup_{x\in M}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(x))-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(x))|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><msup><mi>r</mi><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>data</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq c_{\mu}r^{d^{*}}/2-\sup_{x\in M}|\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(x))-\mu_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{2^{-1/d^{*}}r}(x))|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">Combining this with (<a href="#A3.E20" title="Equation 20 ‣ Proof. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>), we arrive at the bound in the statement.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.4 </span>Weyl’s tube formula</h3>

<div id="A3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The sets <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{r}</annotation></semantics></math> are related to the notion of <span id="A3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">tubes</span> that have been investigated in the differential geometry literature <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray, 2004</a>, <a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Weyl, 1939</a>]</cite>. We borrow a result from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib77" title="" class="ltx_ref">Weyl [1939]</a></cite> that computes the volume enclosing these sets. Let <math id="A3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r}:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\leq r\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r}:=\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}:\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\leq r\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition C.8</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Weyl’s Tube Formula)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose Assumption <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Assumption 3.3. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a> holds, then for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r})=\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})r^{d-d^{*}+2p}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r})=\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})r^{d-d^{*}+2p},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some quantities <math id="A3.Thmtheorem8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The quantities <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{k}</annotation></semantics></math> are related to the integrated mean curvature of <math id="A3.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> and further details about these quantities can be found in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gray, 2004</a>]</cite> where the result is stated in Section 1.1. In this work, we develop upper bounds in such a way that the final result does not depend on these quantities.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Note that using this result, we can obtain estimates for the integrals of functions depending on <math id="A3.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r})</annotation></semantics></math> using the expression,</p>
<table id="A3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}))dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\mathbb{R}^{d}}f(\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}))dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex46.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\frac{d}{dr}\lambda({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r})dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)\frac{d}{dr}\lambda({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{\leq r})dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}(d-d^{*}+2p)\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)r^{d-d^{*}-1+2p}dr." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}(d-d^{*}+2p)\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\int_{0}^{\infty}f(r)r^{d-d^{*}-1+2p}dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs for the main results</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section of the appendix provides the proofs for theorems <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> and <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Geometry-adaptivity and geometric bias ‣ 4 Rethinking the manifold hypothesis: geometry and inductive bias ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. These theorems establish the core result that smoothing in the log-domain is approximately geometry-adaptive, meaning that smoothing with a generic kernel <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> behaves similarly to smoothing with a manifold-adapted kernel <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We begin by proving some lemmas that are involved in the proof of both of these theorems.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Controlling the log-density ratio</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To establish the proximity between <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math> in divergence, we must control the ratio of their densities. In this section, we fix a permissible manifold <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}\in\mathbb{M}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}\in\mathbb{M}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math>, and use <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> as in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Geometric bias of log-domain smoothing ‣ 4 Rethinking the manifold hypothesis: geometry and inductive bias ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. We also fix <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim k_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim k_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Y}=\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}_{r(x)}}(Y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Y}=\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}_{r(x)}}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Y}\sim k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Y}\sim k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the expression in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), we can express the density ratio by,</p>
<table id="A4.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log{\frac{d\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}}{\ d\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|Y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg)-\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]+\log\bigg(\frac{C^{\mathcal{M}}}{C}\bigg)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log{\frac{d\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}}{\ d\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|Y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg)-\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]+\log\bigg(\frac{C^{\mathcal{M}}}{C}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where we define the normalising constants,</p>
<table id="A4.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="C=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}(dy)\bigg)dx,\qquad C^{\mathcal{M}}=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}(dy)\bigg)dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mo>∫</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}(dy)\bigg)dx,\qquad C^{\mathcal{M}}=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}(dy)\bigg)dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">We proceed similarly to the proof in the affine case (see Appendix <a href="#A2" title="Appendix B Manifold-adaptivity in the affine setting ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B</span></a>), decomposing the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LSE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LSE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LSE}</annotation></semantics></math> function into normal and perpendicular components. We use the decomposition,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}=\|y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y)\|^{2}+2\langle y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle+\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}=\|y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y)\|^{2}+2\langle y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle+\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">along with Fact <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> to obtain that,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|Y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|Y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)-\frac{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)-\frac{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">It follows from the definition of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r(x)</annotation></semantics></math> that,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\tilde{Y})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\tilde{Y})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=r(x)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=r(x)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Therefore we may apply Fact <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Fact 3.2. ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> once more to obtain,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|Y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|Y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle+\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle+\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+\Delta_{i}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad=\mathbb{E}\bigg[\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+\Delta_{i}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">where we define the quantity <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}:=2\langle Y-\tilde{Y},\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}:=2\langle Y-\tilde{Y},\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, we obtain the simple expression,</p>
<table id="A4.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log{\frac{d\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}}{\ d\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]+\log\bigg(\frac{C^{\mathcal{M}}}{C}\bigg)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup><mi>C</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log{\frac{d\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}}{\ d\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}}(x)=\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]+\log\bigg(\frac{C^{\mathcal{M}}}{C}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x):=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+\Delta_{i}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)-\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x):=\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+\Delta_{i}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i\in[N]}\bigg)-\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i=1}^{N}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.8" class="ltx_p">Having expressed the log-density ratio in terms of <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, our next task is to bound this quantity. For the sake of intuition, we can consider the linear setting: In this case, <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Y}-Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Y}-Y</annotation></semantics></math> is normal to the manifold and <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is tangent to the manifold, so it would follow that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and thus <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math>. In the case where the manifold is curved, it is no longer necessarily true that <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> and so we control <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> using the curvature of the manifold and the stability of the <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{LSE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>LSE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{LSE}</annotation></semantics></math> function.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with a simple lemma.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}:=\operatorname{dist}(\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},{\mathcal{M}})&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}:=\operatorname{dist}(\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},{\mathcal{M}})&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d},i\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d},i\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math> we have,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta_{i}|\leq\mu_{\epsilon}|\zeta|\Big(\Big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}d_{i}^{2}\Big)\wedge d_{i}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big),\qquad d_{i}=\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta_{i}|\leq\mu_{\epsilon}|\zeta|\Big(\Big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}d_{i}^{2}\Big)\wedge d_{i}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big),\qquad d_{i}=\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where we define the quantity,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta:=\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\mathbb{E}\Big[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta:=\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\mathbb{E}\Big[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the definition of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Y-\tilde{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Y-\tilde{Y}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex60.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y))-(\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y))-(\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y))-\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|}\mathbb{E}\Big[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y))-\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|}\mathbb{E}\Big[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|}\bigg(\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\mathbb{E}\Big[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|}\bigg(\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\mathbb{E}\Big[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">With this, we can write <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> in the following form:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}=2\zeta\bigg\langle\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|},\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\bigg\rangle." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}=2\zeta\bigg\langle\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|},\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\bigg\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">To control <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma C.3. ‣ C.2 Manifold reach ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.3</span></a> as well as the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality to obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\Delta_{i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\Delta_{i}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex63.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\bigg|\zeta\bigg(\bigg\langle\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|},\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\bigg\rangle+\bigg\langle\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|},\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\bigg\rangle\bigg)\bigg|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mi>ζ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\bigg|\zeta\bigg(\bigg\langle\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|},\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\bigg\rangle+\bigg\langle\frac{Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)}{\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|},\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\bigg\rangle\bigg)\bigg|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\mu_{\epsilon}|\zeta|\bigg(\frac{\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\mu_{\epsilon}|\zeta|\bigg(\frac{\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|^{2}}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">completing the proof of the lemma.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> is a random variable, we next find ways of controlling it using <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.2</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\zeta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ζ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\zeta</annotation></semantics></math> be as in Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> and suppose that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[|\zeta|^{2}|S]^{1/2}\leq 2K_{\mathcal{M}},\qquad|\zeta|\leq K^{\max}_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>max</mi></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[|\zeta|^{2}|S]^{1/2}\leq 2K_{\mathcal{M}},\qquad|\zeta|\leq K^{\max}_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">almost surely.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the first bound, we use the <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-triangle inequality to obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\zeta|^{2}|S]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\zeta|^{2}|S]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex65.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big[\big|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\big|^{2}\Big|S\Big]^{1/2}+\big|\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|-\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}|S]^{1/2}\big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big[\big|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\big|^{2}\Big|S\Big]^{1/2}+\big|\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|-\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}|S]^{1/2}\big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big[\big|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\big|^{2}\Big|S\Big]^{1/2}+\mathbb{E}\Big[\Big(\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\Big)^{2}\Big|S\Big]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big[\big|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\big|^{2}\Big|S\Big]^{1/2}+\mathbb{E}\Big[\Big(\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\Big)^{2}\Big|S\Big]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2K_{\mathcal{M}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2K_{\mathcal{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we can obtain <math id="A4.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> bounds via,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\zeta\|_{L^{\infty}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\zeta\|_{L^{\infty}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex68.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Big\|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\Big\|_{L^{\infty}}+\Big\|\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|-\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}|S]^{1/2}\Big\|_{L^{\infty}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo fence="false" lspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0em">+</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Big\|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\Big\|_{L^{\infty}}+\Big\|\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|-\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}|S]^{1/2}\Big\|_{L^{\infty}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now state the bound for <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> that we use for our two main theorems.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.3</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the setting of Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>, then for any <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>, it holds that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{8K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+2\log\big(\tfrac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\big)_{+}+(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\frac{12\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\Big(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{x}\Big)^{2}\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{x}|S)^{1/2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{8K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+2\log\big(\tfrac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\big)_{+}+(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\frac{12\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\Big(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{x}\Big)^{2}\frac{\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{x}|S)^{1/2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S]\Big)_{+}+\Big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S]\Big)_{+}+\Big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for some universal constant <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{C}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>C</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{C}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, where we define <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{x}=\{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{x}=\{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/2\}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x}=\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x}=\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">For this bound, we begin with (<a href="#A3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Stability of the LSE function ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Stability of the LSE function ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex73" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|\leq\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in[N]}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in[N]}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|\leq\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in[N]}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in[N]}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">We decompose this further as,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex74.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbbm{1}_{|I_{1}|&gt;0}\max_{i\in I_{1}}\bigg\{\frac{|\Delta_{i}|}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbbm{1}_{|I_{1}|&gt;0}\max_{i\in I_{1}}\bigg\{\frac{|\Delta_{i}|}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-r\Delta_{i}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=:\mathtt{A}+\mathtt{B}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>𝙰</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝙱</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=:\mathtt{A}+\mathtt{B},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we define the sets,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle I_{0}=\{i\in[N]:\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|\leq\varepsilon_{0}\},\qquad I_{1}=\{i\in[N]:\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|\leq\varepsilon_{1}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle I_{0}=\{i\in[N]:\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|\leq\varepsilon_{0}\},\qquad I_{1}=\{i\in[N]:\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|\leq\varepsilon_{1}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">for some random quantities <math id="A4.SS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0},\varepsilon_{1}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0},\varepsilon_{1}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">The quantity <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{A}</annotation></semantics></math> can be bounded directly using Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>. From this, we obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathtt{A}\leq\frac{\mu_{\epsilon}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}|\zeta|\Big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{1}^{2}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝙰</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathtt{A}\leq\frac{\mu_{\epsilon}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}|\zeta|\Big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{1}^{2}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">To bound <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we proceed with the following upper bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathtt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathtt{B}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex80.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sum_{j\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+|\Delta_{j}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{j}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sum_{j\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+|\Delta_{j}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})|\Delta_{j}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq|I_{0}|^{-1}\max_{i\in I_{0}}\sum_{j\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+|\Delta_{j}|/\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq|I_{0}|^{-1}\max_{i\in I_{0}}\sum_{j\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+|\Delta_{i}|/2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+|\Delta_{j}|/\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used the fact that <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r\leq\exp(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r\leq\exp(r)</annotation></semantics></math>. To further control <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, we control the quantity inside of the exponential function by choosing <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small and <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large so that the quantity in the exponential becomes negative. This allows for control of <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{B}</annotation></semantics></math> by taking <math id="A4.SS1.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start by controlling <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For any <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in I_{0},j\in[N]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in I_{0},j\in[N]</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle-\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}+2\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle-\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad-2\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\rangle." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad-2\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\rangle.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The first term is bounded using the fact that <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\varepsilon_{0}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\varepsilon_{0}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The second term is controlled using the technique from the proof of Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> to deduce the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\big)\wedge\varepsilon_{0}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\big)\wedge\varepsilon_{0}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">where in the second line, we use that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex84.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|^{2}]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex85"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex85.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big[\big|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\big|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}+\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}\Big[\big|\|Y-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)\|-\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|\big|^{2}\Big]^{1/2}+\|x-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(x)\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex86"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex86.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, the fourth term of (<a href="#A4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) is bounded by,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex87"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex87.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\langle\tilde{Y}-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.5.1" class="ltx_text">and finally, the third term of (<a href="#A4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) is controlled using Young’s inequality to obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex88"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex88.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex88.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|^{2}+\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|^{2}+\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex89"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex89.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+2\langle\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+2\langle\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}),\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex90"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex90.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|^{2}-3\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|^{2}-3\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|^{2}-3\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|^{2}-3\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.6.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, substituting (<a href="#A4.E30" title="Equation 30 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>), (<a href="#A4.E31" title="Equation 31 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E32" title="Equation 32 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a>) in to (<a href="#A4.E28" title="Equation 28 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>) leads to the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex91"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex91.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex92"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex92.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}(\varepsilon_{0}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+2\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\big)\wedge\varepsilon_{0}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)-\frac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}+3\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}(\varepsilon_{0}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+2\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\big)\wedge\varepsilon_{0}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)-\frac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}+3\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex93"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex93.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2\mu_{\epsilon}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big(\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex94"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex94.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}K_{\mathcal{M}}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}D_{x}\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-\tfrac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}K_{\mathcal{M}}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}D_{x}\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-\tfrac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\big(\tfrac{1}{2\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\big(\tfrac{1}{2\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.7.1" class="ltx_text">Continuing with bounding the contents of the exponential function in (<a href="#A4.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), we next control <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math>, using Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma D.1. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a> to obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|\leq 2\mu_{\epsilon}|\zeta|\Big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+2\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|+3\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|\leq 2\mu_{\epsilon}|\zeta|\Big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+2\big(\tfrac{1}{2\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|+3\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.8.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, combining (<a href="#A4.E33" title="Equation 33 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E34" title="Equation 34 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a>), we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex95"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex95.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}+|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}+|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex96"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex96.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}(|\zeta|+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+6|\zeta|+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-\tfrac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}(|\zeta|+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+6|\zeta|+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-\tfrac{3}{4}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex97"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex97.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+2(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|)\big(\tfrac{1}{2\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+2(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|)\big(\tfrac{1}{2\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}\big)\wedge\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex98"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex98.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}(|\zeta|+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+6|\zeta|+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-\tfrac{1}{2}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}(|\zeta|+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+6|\zeta|+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-\tfrac{1}{2}\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex99"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex99.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+2\mathbbm{1}_{\mathcal{E}_{x}}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|)\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+2\mathbbm{1}_{\mathcal{E}_{x}}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|)\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{j})\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p9.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p9.9.1" class="ltx_text">where the indicator function contains the event <math id="A4.SS1.p9.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{x}=\{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/4\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≥</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{x}=\{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/4\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using this bound, we choose a value of <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> that guarantees that the contents of the exponential function in (<a href="#A4.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>) is negative.
By solving the quadratic, it follows that to have <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}+|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|\leq-\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>Y</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}-\|\tilde{Y}-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j}\|^{2}+|\Delta_{i}|+2|\Delta_{j}|\leq-\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa</annotation></semantics></math>, for some <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, it is sufficient to have <math id="A4.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\varepsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(Y)-\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}}(\mu_{\epsilon}x_{j})\|\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\varepsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex100"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex100.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{1}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{1}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex100.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=6\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}(|\zeta|+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+6|\zeta|+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=6\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}(|\zeta|+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x})\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+6|\zeta|+4K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+8\mathbbm{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{x}}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|)^{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>x</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+8\mathbbm{1}_{\tilde{\mathcal{E}}_{x}}(K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{x}+2|\zeta|)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting this into (<a href="#A4.E27" title="Equation 27 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), we then obtain the following bound for <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙱</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{B}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex101" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex101.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\mathtt{B}|S]\leq\mathbb{E}\bigg[\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\bigg|S\bigg]\exp(-\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa/2\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>𝙱</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em">]</mo></mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>κ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\mathtt{B}|S]\leq\mathbb{E}\bigg[\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\bigg|S\bigg]\exp(-\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa/2\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">We now return to bounding <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathtt{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝙰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathtt{A}</annotation></semantics></math> with this choice of <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>
to obtain that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex102"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex102.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathtt{A}|S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝙰</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\mathtt{A}|S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex102.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\mu_{\epsilon}K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\bigg(\frac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(6\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{3}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}K_{\mathcal{M}}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}D_{x}\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+16K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>κ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\mu_{\epsilon}K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\bigg(\frac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(6\mu_{\epsilon}\kappa+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(2\mu_{\epsilon}+\tfrac{3}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}K_{\mathcal{M}}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}D_{x}\Big)\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+6\mu_{\epsilon}\Big(5\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+16K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex103"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex103.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+8\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{x}|S)^{1/2}(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{x})^{2}\bigg)+2\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+8\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{x}|S)^{1/2}(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{x})^{2}\bigg)+2\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we utilise the bounds in Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> to control <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\zeta|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\zeta|</annotation></semantics></math>.
We then optimise <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> by choosing,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex104" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex104.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa=\frac{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\mu_{\epsilon}}\log\bigg(\mathbb{E}\Big[|I_{1}^{\complement}|/|I_{0}|\Big|S\Big]\frac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg)_{+}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa=\frac{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}{\mu_{\epsilon}}\log\bigg(\mathbb{E}\Big[|I_{1}^{\complement}|/|I_{0}|\Big|S\Big]\frac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg)_{+},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.4.1" class="ltx_text">which produces the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex105"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex105.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}(x)|S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}(x)|S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex105.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+12\log\Big(\mathbb{E}\Big[|I_{1}^{\complement}|/|I_{0}|\Big|S\Big]\tfrac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big)_{+}+\Big(2+\tfrac{3}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}K_{\mathcal{M}}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}D_{x}\Big)\frac{6\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+12\log\Big(\mathbb{E}\Big[|I_{1}^{\complement}|/|I_{0}|\Big|S\Big]\tfrac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big)_{+}+\Big(2+\tfrac{3}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}K_{\mathcal{M}}+\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}D_{x}\Big)\frac{6\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex106"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex106.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad+\Big(5\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+16K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\frac{6\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{8\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{x}|S)^{1/2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{x})^{2}\bigg)\bigg)+\frac{2K_{\mathcal{M}}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad+\Big(5\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+16K_{\mathcal{M}}+4D_{x}\Big)\frac{6\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{8\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{x}|S)^{1/2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{x})^{2}\bigg)\bigg)+\frac{2K_{\mathcal{M}}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS1.p11.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p11.5.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used that <math id="A4.SS1.p11.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{\epsilon}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{\epsilon}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> to simplify the expression.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">To conclude the proof, we use the fact that <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|I_{0}|=N\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|I_{0}|=N\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon}))</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|I_{1}^{\complement}|\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|I_{1}^{\complement}|\leq N</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, optimising over <math id="A4.SS1.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> leads to the bound in the statement.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The bound on <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> developed in the previous section depends on the distance to the manifold, <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since, for the Rényi divergence, we will integrate <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> with respect to <math id="A4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, we must develop some bounds on the concentration of this measure to the manifold. Due to the complexity of log-domain smoothing, this is non-trivial and relies on Weyl’s formula for the volume of tubular neighbourhoods. In the following lemma, we develop such a concentration inequality.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma D.4</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\essinf_{x\in{\mathcal{M}}}(\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}})_{*}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon}(x))\geq\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi>ess</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>inf</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">B</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\essinf_{x\in{\mathcal{M}}}(\Pi_{{\mathcal{M}}})_{*}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon}(x))\geq\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, then for all <math id="A4.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex107" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex107.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}}(\operatorname{dist}(Z,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq r|S)\leq\exp\bigg(d\log(8)+\frac{5(K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+2\delta^{-1}-\frac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}}(\operatorname{dist}(Z,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq r|S)\leq\exp\bigg(d\log(8)+\frac{5(K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+2\delta^{-1}-\frac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Letting <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we begin by expressing the probability in integral form,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex108" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex108.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\operatorname{dist}(Z,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq r)=C_{\mathcal{M}}^{-1}\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\operatorname{dist}(Z,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq r)=C_{\mathcal{M}}^{-1}\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">From the formulation of <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.1 Warm-up: linear setting ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>), we readily obtain that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex109"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex109.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex109.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\min_{i}\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\log(N)+C_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\min_{i}\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\log(N)+C_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex110"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex110.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\min_{i}\{(\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|-\|\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|)_{+}\}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\log(N)+C_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\frac{\min_{i}\{(\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|-\|\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|)_{+}\}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\log(N)+C_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})_{+}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})_{+}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we use Young’s inequality in the second inequality. Using the fact that <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\in{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{r(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\in{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}_{r(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the following lower bound:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex111"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\operatorname{dist}(" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\operatorname{dist}(</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex111.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle Z,M^{\epsilon})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle Z,M^{\epsilon})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex112"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex112.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex113"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex113.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}))^{2}]^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}))^{2}]^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-K_{\mathcal{M}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-K_{\mathcal{M}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, combining (<a href="#A4.E36" title="Equation 36 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E37" title="Equation 37 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>), we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex114"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex114.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex114.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex115"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex115.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-K_{\mathcal{M}})_{+}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}-K_{\mathcal{M}})_{+}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(-\frac{\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(-\frac{\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we lower bound <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>. For this, we use Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ C.1 Stability of the LSE function ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> with the parameters,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex116" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex116.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{i}=-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}-\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{i}=-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}-\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}x_{i}\|^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">which produces the expression,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex117"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex117.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex117.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+(\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|-\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}))+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)+C_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>LSE</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\operatorname{LSE}\bigg(\bigg\{-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+(\|y-\mu_{\epsilon}\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\|-\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}))+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}_{i}\bigg)+C_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex118"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex118.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})}+\log(N)+C_{\epsilon}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i=1}^{N}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})}+\log(N)+C_{\epsilon}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">We control this further using a similar technique to that used in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>. We define the sets <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="I_{0}=\{i\in[N]:\epsilon_{i}\geq-\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}/\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\},I_{1}=\{i\in[N]:\epsilon_{i}\geq-2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}/\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{0}=\{i\in[N]:\epsilon_{i}\geq-\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}/\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\},I_{1}=\{i\in[N]:\epsilon_{i}\geq-2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}/\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> for any quantity <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. With this, we obtain the following bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex119"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex119.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex119.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})}dr+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})}dr-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i\in I_{1}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})}dr+\int_{0}^{1}\frac{\sum_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})\epsilon_{i}}{\sum_{i\in I_{0}}\exp(r\epsilon_{i})}dr-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex120"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex120.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\min_{i\in I_{1}}\epsilon_{i}+\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\int_{0}^{1}\min_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement},j\in I_{0}}\exp(r(\epsilon_{i}-\epsilon_{j}))\epsilon_{i}dr-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\min_{i\in I_{1}}\epsilon_{i}+\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\int_{0}^{1}\min_{i\in I_{1}^{\complement},j\in I_{0}}\exp(r(\epsilon_{i}-\epsilon_{j}))\epsilon_{i}dr-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex121"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex121.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\int_{0}^{1}\exp\bigg(-\frac{r\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\frac{2\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}dr-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\int_{0}^{1}\exp\bigg(-\frac{r\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\frac{2\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}dr-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">This is further controlled using the fact that <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{0}\supseteq\{i\in[N]:\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(y/\mu_{\epsilon})\|^{2}\leq\varepsilon^{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>⊇</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{0}\supseteq\{i\in[N]:\|\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})-\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(y/\mu_{\epsilon})\|^{2}\leq\varepsilon^{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|I_{1}^{\complement}|\leq N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|I_{1}^{\complement}|\leq N</annotation></semantics></math> and hence</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex122" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex122.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\leq\frac{N}{|\{\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}\cap B_{\varepsilon}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(y/\mu_{\epsilon}))|}\leq\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}\leq\delta^{-1}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>∁</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>∩</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{|I_{1}^{\complement}|}{|I_{0}|}\leq\frac{N}{|\{\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(x_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}\cap B_{\varepsilon}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(y/\mu_{\epsilon}))|}\leq\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}\leq\delta^{-1},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the last inequality holds almost surely. In combination with the bound <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{dist}(Z,M^{\epsilon})^{2}]\leq 2\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}+2K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\operatorname{dist}(Z,M^{\epsilon})^{2}]\leq 2\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}+2K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E39" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-2\delta^{-1}-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)\geq-\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-2\delta^{-1}-\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">With this, we lower bound <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> by,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex123"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex123.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex123.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\geq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\int\exp\bigg(-\frac{2\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}+2(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-2\delta^{-1}\bigg)dx." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\int\exp\bigg(-\frac{2\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{2}+2(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-2\delta^{-1}\bigg)dx.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Before combining the bounds in (<a href="#A4.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E40" title="Equation 40 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">40</span></a>) we further simplify their expressions using Weyl’s formula (see Section <a href="#A3.SS4" title="C.4 Weyl’s tube formula ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>). Combining the bound in (<a href="#A4.E38" title="Equation 38 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">38</span></a>) with the integral formula in (<a href="#A3.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ C.4 Weyl’s tube formula ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>), we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex124"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex124.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex125"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex125.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\bigg(\frac{(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}(d-d^{*}+2p)\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\int_{r}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(-\frac{s^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)s^{d-d^{*}-1+2p}ds." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\bigg(\frac{(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}(d-d^{*}+2p)\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\int_{r}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(-\frac{s^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)s^{d-d^{*}-1+2p}ds.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The integral on the right-hand side can be analysed by relating it to the measure of a related spherically symmetric measure (e.g. see equation (4) in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bobkov [2003]</a></cite>). With this we relate the integral to the concentration of a Gaussian random variable:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex126"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex126.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{r}^{\infty}s^{k-1}\exp(-s^{2}/4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})ds" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mi>r</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msup><mi>s</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msup><mi>s</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>s</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{r}^{\infty}s^{k-1}\exp(-s^{2}/4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})ds</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex126.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\Gamma(k/2+1)}{k\pi^{k/2}}\int_{\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{k}:\|x\|\geq r\}}\exp(-\|x\|^{2}/4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>π</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>k</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub></mstyle><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>x</mi><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mn>4</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\Gamma(k/2+1)}{k\pi^{k/2}}\int_{\{x\in\mathbb{R}^{k}:\|x\|\geq r\}}\exp(-\|x\|^{2}/4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex127"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex127.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\Gamma(k/2+1)(4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{k/2}}{k}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{k})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>k</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\Gamma(k/2+1)(4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{k/2}}{k}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{k})}(\|\xi\|\geq r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we obtain the expression,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_gather ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex128"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex128.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx=(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\Big(\tfrac{(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big)\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}w_{p}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\operatorname{dist}(\cdot,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r}\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}^{\mathcal{M}}(dy)\bigg)dx=(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\Big(\tfrac{(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big)\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}w_{p}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex129"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex129.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle w_{p}:=\frac{\Gamma((d-d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}+2p)/2+1)(4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{(d-d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}+2p)/2}}{d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p}(d-d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}+2p)\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>k</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle w_{p}:=\frac{\Gamma((d-d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}+2p)/2+1)(4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{(d-d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}+2p)/2}}{d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p}(d-d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}+2p)\tilde{k}_{2p}({\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">By a similar argument, we also obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex130"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex130.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{M}}\geq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\bigg(-\frac{4(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-2\delta^{-1}\bigg)\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}64^{-(d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p)/2}w_{p}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msup><mn>64</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C_{\mathcal{M}}\geq(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d/2}\exp\bigg(-\frac{4(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}-2\delta^{-1}\bigg)\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}64^{-(d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p)/2}w_{p}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Dividing the two, we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex131"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex131.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex131.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(\operatorname{dist}(Z,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(\operatorname{dist}(Z,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})\geq r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex132"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex132.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}w_{p}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)}{\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}/2\rfloor}64^{-(d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p)/2}w_{p}}\exp\bigg(\frac{5(K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+2\delta^{-1}\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>w</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∑</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></msup><mn>64</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mi>w</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor}w_{p}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)}{\sum_{p=0}^{\lfloor d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}/2\rfloor}64^{-(d-d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}+2p)/2}w_{p}}\exp\bigg(\frac{5(K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+2\delta^{-1}\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex133"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex133.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 8^{d}\exp\bigg(\frac{5(K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+2\delta^{-1}\bigg)\max_{p\in\{0,...,\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor\}}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{d-d^{*}+2p})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>8</mn><mi>d</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><munder><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 8^{d}\exp\bigg(\frac{5(K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}+\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\frac{2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+2\delta^{-1}\bigg)\max_{p\in\{0,...,\lfloor d^{*}/2\rfloor\}}\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{d-d^{*}+2p})}(\|\xi\|\geq r).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">We then bound this further using the concentration of the chi-squared distribution (see Example 2.28 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib74" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wainwright, 2019</a>]</cite>), obtaining</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex134"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex134.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{k})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{\xi\sim N(0,2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}I_{k})}(\|\xi\|\geq r)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex134.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\bigg(-\frac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}k})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\bigg(-\frac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}k})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex135"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex135.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\bigg(-\frac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\bigg(-\frac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">completing the proof of the bound.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With the pointwise bounds on <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]</annotation></semantics></math> from the previous subsection, we are now prepared to derive the Rényi divergence bound in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">To bound the Rényi divergence, we begin with the following expression which follows from (<a href="#A4.E24" title="Equation 24 ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex136"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex136.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{q}(\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}\|\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{q}(\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}\|\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex136.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int\bigg(\frac{\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(x)}{\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}(x)}\bigg)^{q-1}\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int\bigg(\frac{\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(x)}{\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}(x)}\bigg)^{q-1}\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex137"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex137.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int\exp((q-1)\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S])\,\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)+\log(C^{\mathcal{M}}/C)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{q-1}\log\int\exp((q-1)\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S])\,\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)+\log(C^{\mathcal{M}}/C),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the normalisation constants, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C^{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C^{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, are as defined in (<a href="#A4.E23" title="Equation 23 ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>). Furthermore, we obtain the following relationship between the normalisation constants:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex138"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex138.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex138.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}(dy)-\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}(dy)+\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}(dy)\bigg)dx" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo lspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}(dy)-\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}(dy)+\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k^{\mathcal{M}}_{x}(dy)\bigg)dx</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex139"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex139.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=C^{\mathcal{M}}\int\exp(\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S])\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=C^{\mathcal{M}}\int\exp(\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S])\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, using Jensen’s inequality, we deduce the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex140"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex140.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle D_{q}(\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}\|\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle D_{q}(\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}\|\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex140.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\beta}\log\int\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]|)\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{2}{\beta}\log\int\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(x)|S]|)\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">where, for the sake of brevity, we use the shorthand <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=(q-1)\vee 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=(q-1)\vee 1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">We proceed by applying the bound on <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> developed in Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>. The assumptions of Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a> hold with <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}=0</annotation></semantics></math> and hence, we have the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex141"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex141.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex141.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{16K}{\tau}\bigg(1+\log\Big(\frac{\tau}{K}\Big)_{+}+\frac{(5K_{\max}^{1/2}K^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{16K}{\tau}\bigg(1+\log\Big(\frac{\tau}{K}\Big)_{+}+\frac{(5K_{\max}^{1/2}K^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E42.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad+\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\bigg)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad+\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we have used the fact that <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\zeta|\leq 2K_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ζ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\zeta|\leq 2K_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, (see Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma D.2. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>) and therefore, <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{Z}|S,Z)^{1/2}\leq\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}(\mathcal{E}_{Z}|S,Z)^{1/2}\leq\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}</annotation></semantics></math>. To control the infimum term, we utilise the bound on balls of <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}</annotation></semantics></math> given in Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>. In this lemma, it is shown that whenever <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, with probability <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{y\in{\mathcal{M}}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(y))^{-1}\leq c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}/4," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{y\in{\mathcal{M}}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(y))^{-1}\leq c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}/4,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">once <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large so that the condition in (<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is satisfied with <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Indeed, there exists a value <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}\in(0,\tau/64]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}\in(0,\tau/64]</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying this condition as soon as we assume that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq 64\Big((144d^{*}\log(128/\tau)+144\log(2/c_{\mu}))\vee\tfrac{\log(\delta^{-1})}{2}\Big)(\tau/64)^{-2d^{*}}c_{\mu}^{-2}=:N_{\min}(d^{*},\tau,\delta,c_{\mu})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>64</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>144</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>128</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>144</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq 64\Big((144d^{*}\log(128/\tau)+144\log(2/c_{\mu}))\vee\tfrac{\log(\delta^{-1})}{2}\Big)(\tau/64)^{-2d^{*}}c_{\mu}^{-2}=:N_{\min}(d^{*},\tau,\delta,c_{\mu}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">If we set <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}^{2}=d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}^{2}=d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and require that <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq(\tau/64)^{2}/d^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq(\tau/64)^{2}/d^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, then once <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large so that (<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is satisfied, we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex142"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex142.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{Z}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{Z}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex143"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex143.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\leq\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/64]}\sup_{y\in{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg\{\log\big(\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(y))^{-1}\big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="4.278em" rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.0835em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.0835em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\leq\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}\in(0,\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/64]}\sup_{y\in{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg\{\log\big(\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(y))^{-1}\big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\lesssim\Big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\Big)d^{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="4.278em">≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\lesssim\Big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\Big)d^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Indeed, this would require <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\gtrsim(d^{*}+1)c_{\mu}^{-2}(d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≳</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\gtrsim(d^{*}+1)c_{\mu}^{-2}(d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})^{-d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> does not satisfy this, then we instead set <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the smallest <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> such that (<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is satisfied, arriving at a quantity with <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m18" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}\lesssim\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\lesssim(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo>≲</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≲</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}\lesssim\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\lesssim(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{*}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{*}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon^{2}_{0}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon^{2}_{0}=0</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d^{*}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d^{*}=0</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus, we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{Z}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\lesssim 1+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{d^{*}&gt;0}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{Z}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\lesssim 1+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{d^{*}&gt;0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">We can then combine the bounds in (<a href="#A4.E45" title="Equation 45 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E46" title="Equation 46 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">46</span></a>), to obtain that there exists a quantity <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> that depends only logarithmically on structural parameters and satisfies,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E47.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\leq C_{2}\bigg(1+\Big(1+\tfrac{D_{Z}}{\tau}\Big)d^{*}\vee((c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{-2})\bigg)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∨</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)_{+}+\big(1+\tfrac{K+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\leq C_{2}\bigg(1+\Big(1+\tfrac{D_{Z}}{\tau}\Big)d^{*}\vee((c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{-2})\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">where we have also used the fact that <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leq K_{\max}\leq\tau/96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leq K_{\max}\leq\tau/96</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Returning to bounding (<a href="#A4.E41" title="Equation 41 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">41</span></a>), we use (<a href="#A4.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E47" title="Equation 47 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>) to derive the upper bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex144"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex144.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex145"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex145.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\Big[\exp\Big(\tfrac{8\beta K}{\tau}\Big(1+2\log\big(\tfrac{\tau}{K}\big)_{+}+\tfrac{(5K_{\max}^{1/2}K^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}+C_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>log</mi><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\Big[\exp\Big(\tfrac{8\beta K}{\tau}\Big(1+2\log\big(\tfrac{\tau}{K}\big)_{+}+\tfrac{(5K_{\max}^{1/2}K^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}+C_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex146"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex146.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\quad+C_{2}\Big(1+\tfrac{D_{Z}}{\tau}\Big)d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big)\Big)\Big|S\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\quad+C_{2}\Big(1+\tfrac{D_{Z}}{\tau}\Big)d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big)\Big)\Big|S\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex147"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex147.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{16K}{\tau}\bigg(1+2\log\big(\frac{\tau}{K}\big)+C_{2}+C_{2}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)+\frac{1}{20\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40\beta K}{\tau}\tfrac{C_{2}D_{Z}}{\tau}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>τ</mi><mi>K</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\leq\frac{16K}{\tau}\bigg(1+2\log\big(\frac{\tau}{K}\big)+C_{2}+C_{2}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)+\frac{1}{20\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40\beta K}{\tau}\tfrac{C_{2}D_{Z}}{\tau}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\quad\qquad+\frac{1}{5\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\quad\qquad+\frac{1}{5\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">where in the second inequality, we use Hölder’s inequality.
We now bound the last two terms, starting with the second.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We utilise Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> which we apply with <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=\tau/64" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\tau/64</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result of (<a href="#A4.E43" title="Equation 43 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>) and the assumed lower bound on <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>, the assumptions of Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> are satisfied with <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=c_{\mu}(\tau/64)^{d^{*}}/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=c_{\mu}(\tau/64)^{d^{*}}/4</annotation></semantics></math>, and so, for any <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex148"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex148.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq r|S)\leq\exp\Big(C-\tfrac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big),\qquad C:=\log(8)d+\frac{5K^{2}+2^{-10}\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\tau^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq r|S)\leq\exp\Big(C-\tfrac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big),\qquad C:=\log(8)d+\frac{5K^{2}+2^{-10}\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\tau^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, for any <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c,R&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c,R&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex149"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex149.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big[\exp\big(cD_{Z}\big)\big|S\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\big[\exp\big(cD_{Z}\big)\big|S\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex149.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\log(r)/c)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\log(r)/c)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex150"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex150.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\exp(cR)+\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\log(r)/c)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\exp(cR)+\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\log(r)/c)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex151"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex151.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\exp(cR)+\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(\log(r)/c-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dr." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\exp(cR)+\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(\log(r)/c-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">This is simplified using the change of variables,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex152"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex152.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(\log(r)/c-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(\log(r)/c-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex152.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(u+R-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+c(u+R)\bigg)du." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(u+R-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+c(u+R)\bigg)du.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">We then choose <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:=\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+16c\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sqrt{256c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{4}+32\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>256</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:=\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+16c\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+\sqrt{256c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{4}+32\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C}</annotation></semantics></math> to further simplify the expression, obtaining,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex153"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex153.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(\log(r)/c-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{32c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\exp(cR)}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{(\log(r)/c-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{32c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex153.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=c\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(-\frac{u^{2}}{32\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+u\bigg(c-\frac{R}{16\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)+c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\bigg)du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>R</mi><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=c\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(-\frac{u^{2}}{32\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+u\bigg(c-\frac{R}{16\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)+c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\bigg)du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex154"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex154.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq c\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(-\frac{u^{2}}{32\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)du" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq c\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})\int_{0}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(-\frac{u^{2}}{32\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)du</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex155"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex155.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(32\pi)^{1/2}\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c\sigma_{\epsilon}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(32\pi)^{1/2}\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c\sigma_{\epsilon},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the last line follows from the Gaussian integral. With this, we obtain a bound on the MGF:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex156"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex156.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\big[\exp\big(cD_{Z}\big)\big|S\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\big[\exp\big(cD_{Z}\big)\big|S\big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex156.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\log\big(\exp(cR)+(32\pi)^{1/2}\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c\sigma_{\epsilon}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\log\big(\exp(cR)+(32\pi)^{1/2}\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c\sigma_{\epsilon}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex157"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex157.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq cR+\log\big(1+(32\pi)^{1/2}\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}-cR)c\sigma_{\epsilon}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq cR+\log\big(1+(32\pi)^{1/2}\exp(c\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}-cR)c\sigma_{\epsilon}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex158"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex158.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq cR+(32\pi)^{1/2}c\sigma_{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>32</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq cR+(32\pi)^{1/2}c\sigma_{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex159"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex159.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+c(K+\tau)+c\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+c(K+\tau)+c\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.6.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting values for <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex160"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex160.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{20\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{20\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex160.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40\beta K}{\tau}\tfrac{C_{2}D_{Z}}{\tau}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40\beta K}{\tau}\tfrac{C_{2}D_{Z}}{\tau}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex161"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex161.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\frac{K}{\tau^{2}}\bigg(d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg(\tau+\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})+\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\frac{K}{\tau^{2}}\bigg(d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\frac{K}{\tau^{2}}\bigg(d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg(\tau+\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})+\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\frac{K}{\tau^{2}}\bigg(d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E49.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\frac{K}{\tau}\bigg(d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg(1+\frac{\sigma_{\epsilon}}{\tau}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})+\frac{K}{\tau^{3}}\bigg((\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d^{*})\vee\tau^{2}\bigg)\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>∨</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\frac{K}{\tau}\bigg(d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg(1+\frac{\sigma_{\epsilon}}{\tau}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})+\frac{K}{\tau^{3}}\bigg((\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d^{*})\vee\tau^{2}\bigg)\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.7.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, as soon as we require that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex162" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex162.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq\Big(\frac{K^{2}}{d\tau^{2}}\Big)\wedge\frac{\tau^{2}}{(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})^{2}}\wedge\Big(\frac{\tau^{2}}{d^{*}}\Big)=:\sigma_{\max,1}^{2}(d,d^{*},\tau,K,c_{\mu})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq\Big(\frac{K^{2}}{d\tau^{2}}\Big)\wedge\frac{\tau^{2}}{(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})^{2}}\wedge\Big(\frac{\tau^{2}}{d^{*}}\Big)=:\sigma_{\max,1}^{2}(d,d^{*},\tau,K,c_{\mu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.8.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{20\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40\beta K}{\tau}\tfrac{C_{2}D_{Z}}{\tau}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K}{\tau}\bigg((d^{*}+1)\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∨</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{20\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40\beta K}{\tau}\tfrac{C_{2}D_{Z}}{\tau}d^{*}\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K}{\tau}\bigg((d^{*}+1)\vee\tfrac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now bound the third term of (<a href="#A4.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>). We once again use the integral formula for the expectation to obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex163"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex163.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex163.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex164"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex164.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg(\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\geq r\bigg|S\bigg)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg(\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\geq r\bigg|S\bigg)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex165"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex165.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K_{\max}+D_{Z})^{2}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\int_{0}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K_{\max}+D_{Z})^{2}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex166"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex166.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=1+\Big(\exp\Big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\Big)-1\Big)\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4-5K_{\max}|S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=1+\Big(\exp\Big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\Big)-1\Big)\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4-5K_{\max}|S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\int_{\exp\big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\big)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\int_{\exp\big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\big)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">We further bound the last term using <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K\leq K_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K\leq K_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> along with a change of variables, to derive,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex167"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex167.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int_{\exp\big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\big)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K_{\max}+D_{Z})^{2}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.100em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int_{\exp\big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\big)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K_{\max}+D_{Z})^{2}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex168"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex168.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq u|S)\exp\bigg(\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}(5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq u|S)\exp\bigg(\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex169"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex169.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(u-5K_{\max}-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\big)^{2}+\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(u-5K_{\max}-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\big)^{2}+\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">Setting <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=1-\frac{40\beta K}{\tau}&gt;1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=1-\frac{40\beta K}{\tau}&gt;1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, we can simplify this expression by,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex170"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex170.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(u-5K_{\max}-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\big)^{2}+\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(u-5K_{\max}-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\big)^{2}+\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex171"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex171.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad=\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{c}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(u-(5K_{\max}+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c^{-1}\bigg)^{2}+\frac{1-c^{-1}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}(5K_{\max}+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}\bigg)udu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad=\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{c}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(u-(5K_{\max}+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c^{-1}\bigg)^{2}+\frac{1-c^{-1}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}(5K_{\max}+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}\bigg)udu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex172"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex172.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\pi/c)^{1/2}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{c}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4-(5K_{\max}+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c^{-1}\bigg)^{2}\bigg)\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}/c}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\pi/c)^{1/2}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{c}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4-(5K_{\max}+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})c^{-1}\bigg)^{2}\bigg)\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}/c},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.4.1" class="ltx_text">where the final inequality follows from the concentration of the Gaussian random variable. Using the fact that <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\max}\leq\tau/96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\max}\leq\tau/96</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c^{-1}\leq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>c</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c^{-1}\leq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and assuming that <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq\frac{K_{\max}^{2}}{2d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq\frac{K_{\max}^{2}}{2d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex173"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex173.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(u-5K_{\max}-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\big)^{2}+\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{20\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}\int_{\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}^{\infty}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(u-5K_{\max}-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}\big)^{2}+\frac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}u^{2}\bigg)udu</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex174"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex174.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{40\sqrt{2\pi}\beta K}{\tau c}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/8\big)^{2}\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{40\sqrt{2\pi}\beta K}{\tau c}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/8\big)^{2}\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.5.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we can bound the second term of (<a href="#A4.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>), in total, obtaining,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex175"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex175.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{1}{5\beta}\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{1}{5\beta}\log</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex175.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex176"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex176.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\Big(\exp\Big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\Big)-1\Big)\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4-5K_{\max}|S)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ℙ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\Big(\exp\Big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\Big)-1\Big)\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4-5K_{\max}|S)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex177"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex177.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\int_{\exp\big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\big)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle scriptlevel="-1"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\int_{\exp\big(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}\big)}^{\infty}\mathbb{P}\bigg((5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}\geq\frac{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}{10\beta K}\log(r)\bigg|S\bigg)dr</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex178"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex178.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\exp\bigg(C+\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(3\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/16\big)^{2}\bigg)+\frac{K}{\tau}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/8\big)^{2}\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\exp\bigg(C+\tfrac{10\beta K}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}\tau}(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4)^{2}-\frac{1}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(3\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/16\big)^{2}\bigg)+\frac{K}{\tau}\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/8\big)^{2}\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex179"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex179.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/8\big)^{2}\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\exp\bigg(C-\frac{1}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\big(\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/8\big)^{2}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.6.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, by requiring that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex180" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex180.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq 2^{10}\Big(\log(8)d+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}\Big)\log(\tau/K)=:\sigma^{2}_{\max,2}(d^{*},d,\tau,K,c_{\mu})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>10</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq 2^{10}\Big(\log(8)d+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}\Big)\log(\tau/K)=:\sigma^{2}_{\max,2}(d^{*},d,\tau,K,c_{\mu}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.7.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain the upper bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{5\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K}{\tau}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{5\beta}\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10\beta K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K}{\tau}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.8.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, by substituting (<a href="#A4.E50" title="Equation 50 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">50</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E52" title="Equation 52 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) into (<a href="#A4.E48" title="Equation 48 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">48</span></a>) we obtain that, with a probability of at least <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex181" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex181.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]\lesssim\frac{K}{\tau}\max\bigg\{d^{*}+1,\frac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>β</mi></mfrac><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mfrac><mi>K</mi><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mfrac></mrow></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{2}{\beta}\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(\beta|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]\lesssim\frac{K}{\tau}\max\bigg\{d^{*}+1,\frac{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.9.1" class="ltx_text">completing the proof. We collect the required upper bounds on <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, which when combined with the fact that <math id="A4.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≤</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\leq\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, leads to the sufficient condition,</span></p>
<table id="A4.E53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\leq\sigma_{\max,1}^{2}(d,d^{*},\tau,K,c_{\mu})\wedge\sigma^{2}_{\max,2}(d^{*},d,\tau,K,c_{\mu})\wedge\frac{K^{2}_{\max}}{2d}\wedge\frac{\tau^{2}}{(64)^{2}d^{*}}=:\epsilon_{\max}(d,d^{*},\tau,K,K_{\max},c_{\mu})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∧</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>∧</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\leq\sigma_{\max,1}^{2}(d,d^{*},\tau,K,c_{\mu})\wedge\sigma^{2}_{\max,2}(d^{*},d,\tau,K,c_{\mu})\wedge\frac{K^{2}_{\max}}{2d}\wedge\frac{\tau^{2}}{(64)^{2}d^{*}}=:\epsilon_{\max}(d,d^{*},\tau,K,K_{\max},c_{\mu}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.10.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ 4.2 Geometry-adaptivity and geometric bias ‣ 4 Rethinking the manifold hypothesis: geometry and inductive bias ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h3>

<div id="A4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}\in\mathbbm{M}_{\mu}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>𝕄</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}\in\mathbbm{M}_{\mu}</annotation></semantics></math> and let <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\mathcal{M}},d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}},\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\mathcal{M}},d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\mathcal{M}},K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}},\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\mu,{\mathcal{M}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\mu,{\mathcal{M}}}</annotation></semantics></math> be as defined in Section <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Geometric bias of log-domain smoothing ‣ 4 Rethinking the manifold hypothesis: geometry and inductive bias ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and we assume <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}\leq\tau/96" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>96</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}\leq\tau/96</annotation></semantics></math>. Using the same argument that produced (<a href="#A4.E42" title="Equation 42 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>), we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex182" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex182.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{2}(\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}\|\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}})\leq 2\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{2}(\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}\|\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}})\leq 2\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z\sim\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}(dx)</annotation></semantics></math>. Using Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma D.3. ‣ D.1 Controlling the log-density ratio ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, we obtain pointwise bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex183"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex183.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[|\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex184"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex184.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{8C_{1}K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+2\log\big(\tfrac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\big)+\frac{(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{D_{Z}\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}+\Big(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}\Big)\frac{12\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>12</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{8C_{1}K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+2\log\big(\tfrac{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}{K_{\mathcal{M}}}\big)+\frac{(5K_{\max,{\mathcal{M}}}^{1/2}K_{\mathcal{M}}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\mathbbm{1}_{D_{Z}\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}+\Big(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}\Big)\frac{12\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex185"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex185.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)+\big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)+\big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}}{\tau}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">To bound the term with the infimum, we proceed similarly to the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>, bounding it using Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>. Given that <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently large, we obtain from this lemma that,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex186" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex186.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{y\in{\mathcal{M}}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(x))^{-1}\leq c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}/4,\qquad\text{ for all }r\in[\sqrt{d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\wedge(K/2),\tau]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{y\in{\mathcal{M}}}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(x))^{-1}\leq c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}/4,\qquad\text{ for all }r\in[\sqrt{d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\wedge(K/2),\tau],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">with probability <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. With this we can choose <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}^{2}=d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}^{2}=d^{*}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain the upper bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex187" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex187.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{Z}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)+\big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\leq C_{3}\bigg(1+\Big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}\bigg)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>log</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\inf_{\varepsilon_{0}&gt;0}\bigg\{\log\Big(\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{Z}}[\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\varepsilon_{0}}(\Pi_{\mathcal{M}}(Y/\mu_{\epsilon})))^{-1}|S,Z]\Big)+\big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\big)\frac{\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg\}\leq C_{3}\bigg(1+\Big(1+\tfrac{K_{\mathcal{M}}+D_{Z}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}\bigg),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">for some quantity <math id="A4.SS4.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> which depends only logarithmically on structural parameters. With this, we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex188"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex188.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle 2\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex189"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+\Big(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+d^{*}\bigg)+\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{C_{3}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}D_{Z}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≲</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+\Big(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+d^{*}\bigg)+\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{C_{3}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}D_{Z}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mi>τ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad+\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10K}{\tau}\frac{(5K^{1/2}K_{\max}^{1/2}+D_{Z})^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{5K_{\max}+D_{Z}\geq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We bound the second and third terms similarly to as in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>. However, the concentration of <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> differs slightly due to the additional error from <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. We apply Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a> with <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=K/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=K/2</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain that for any <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex190"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq r|S)\leq\exp\Big(C-\tfrac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}(D_{Z}\geq r|S)\leq\exp\Big(C-\tfrac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">for all <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d</annotation></semantics></math>, where the constant is given by</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex191"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex191.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\big(\tfrac{1}{8}+\log(32)\big)d+\tfrac{5(K+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+K^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>32</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\big(\tfrac{1}{8}+\log(32)\big)d+\tfrac{5(K+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}+K^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex192"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\big(\tfrac{1}{8}+\log(32)\big)d+\tfrac{6(K+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>32</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\big(\tfrac{1}{8}+\log(32)\big)d+\tfrac{6(K+\mu_{\epsilon}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}})^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">To bound the third term of (<a href="#A4.E54" title="Equation 54 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>), we can directly use the argument in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> that produces (<a href="#A4.E51" title="Equation 51 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>). Indeed, taking <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small, we obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex193" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\tfrac{D_{Z}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{D_{Z}\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{10K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\tfrac{D_{Z}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\mathbbm{1}_{D_{Z}\leq\mu_{\epsilon}\tau_{\mathcal{M}}/4}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, we can borrow the argument that produces (<a href="#A4.E49" title="Equation 49 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>), to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex194"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{C_{3}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}D_{Z}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{C_{3}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}D_{Z}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex195"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+cK_{\mathcal{M}}+c\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+c^{2}\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}+cK_{\mathcal{M}}+c\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex196"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}\bigg(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})+\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}\bigg(K_{\mathcal{M}}+\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\sigma_{\epsilon}(\sqrt{d}+c_{\mu}^{-1/2}(\tau/64)^{-d^{*}/2})+\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">With this, we obtain that as soon as <math id="A4.SS4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is sufficiently small, we obtain,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex197" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{C_{3}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}D_{Z}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(\frac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\bigg)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>40</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false" maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\mathbb{E}\bigg[\exp\bigg(\tfrac{40K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Big(\tfrac{C_{3}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\tfrac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\Big)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}D_{Z}\bigg)\bigg|S\bigg]\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(\frac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\bigg)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, returning to (<a href="#A4.E54" title="Equation 54 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.4 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">54</span></a>) we obtain the bound,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle 2\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>log</mi><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><msub><mi>LSE</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\log\mathbb{E}[\exp(|\mathbb{E}[\Delta\operatorname{LSE}_{\mathcal{M}}(Z)|S,Z]|)|S]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+\Big(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+d^{*}\bigg)+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(\frac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\bigg)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\leq\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(1+\Big(\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}+\tau_{\mathcal{M}}+K_{\mathcal{M}}\Big)\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+d^{*}\bigg)+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\bigg(\frac{1}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\frac{\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}^{2}}{\sigma^{2}_{\epsilon}}\bigg)d_{\mathcal{M}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}(d^{*}+1)}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(1+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">≲</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\lesssim\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}(d^{*}+1)}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\bigg(1+\frac{K_{\mathcal{M}}d^{*}_{\mathcal{M}}}{\tau_{\mathcal{M}}}\Delta_{\mathcal{M}}\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.p2.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.p2.7.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proofs of other results</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix contains the proofs for Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 3.7. ‣ 3.3 Log-domain smoothing and generalisation ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a> and Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem8" title="Proposition 3.8. ‣ 3.3 Log-domain smoothing and generalisation ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a>. These results further elucidate the desirable properties of log-domain smoothing, specifically regarding how it concentrates mass near the manifold and distributes mass along it.</p>
</div>
<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Proof of Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 3.7. ‣ 3.3 Log-domain smoothing and generalisation ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To prove this corollary, we utilise Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>. As remarked in the proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>, there exists a <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}\in[0,\tau/16]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}\in[0,\tau/16]</annotation></semantics></math> such that with a probability of at least <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain with probability bound,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{Y\sim\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r|S)\leq\exp\Big(C-\tfrac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big),\qquad C:=\log(8)d+\tfrac{5K^{2}+4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>8</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{Y\sim\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r|S)\leq\exp\Big(C-\tfrac{(r-\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d})^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big),\qquad C:=\log(8)d+\tfrac{5K^{2}+4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{2}\geq 4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> must be chosen according to the size of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> and the condition in (<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>). In particular, we have the bound,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex202" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}_{Y\sim\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C^{2}}|S)\leq\exp\Big(-\tfrac{r^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}_{Y\sim\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon}}(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C^{2}}|S)\leq\exp\Big(-\tfrac{r^{2}}{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">When <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is large enough, we choose the optimal value of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}^{2}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}^{2}=\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex203" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\bigg(\tfrac{4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}\bigg)\lesssim\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\bigg(\tfrac{4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}\bigg)\lesssim\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">If <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is not sufficiently large, we choose <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be the smallest value such that (<a href="#A3.E19" title="Equation 19 ‣ Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>) is satisfied, yielding <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}\lesssim\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\lesssim(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo>≲</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>≲</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}\lesssim\varepsilon_{0}^{2}\lesssim(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}</annotation></semantics></math> and also,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex204" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\bigg(\tfrac{4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}\bigg)\lesssim(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≲</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\bigg(\tfrac{4\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}}{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+8c_{\mu}^{-1}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}\bigg)\lesssim(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">With these choices of <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain the bound,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex205" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C}\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+K+\max\{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/2d^{*}},\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}+2}}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>≲</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C}\lesssim\sqrt{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+K+\max\{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/2d^{*}},\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{1}{d^{*}+2}}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Next we transfer this concentration property to the measure <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{p}_{\epsilon}^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> by utilising the bound Rényi divergence bound in Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a>. By utilising Lemma 21 of <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chewi et al. [2022]</a></cite>, we obtain the bound,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex206"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{Y\sim\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}}\Big(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C^{2}}+\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}D_{2}(\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}\|\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon})}\Big|S\Big)\leq 2\exp\Big(-\tfrac{r^{2}}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ℙ</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>k</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>k</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></msup></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.600em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>S</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>r</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{P}_{Y\sim\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}}\Big(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}})\geq r+\sqrt{2\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}d}+\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}C^{2}}+\sqrt{4\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}D_{2}(\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}\|\hat{p}^{k^{\mathcal{M}}}_{\epsilon})}\Big|S\Big)\leq 2\exp\Big(-\tfrac{r^{2}}{8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.7" class="ltx_p">Finally we use Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem6" title="Theorem 3.6. ‣ 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.6</span></a> to bound the <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2</annotation></semantics></math>-Rényi divergence with probability at least <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Proof of Proposition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem8" title="Proposition 3.8. ‣ 3.3 Log-domain smoothing and generalisation ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.8</span></a></h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, choose and let <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma^{i}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma^{i}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> be the shortest constant velocity path on the manifold <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math> connecting points <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Choose <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt</annotation></semantics></math> is minimised, i.e. the closest example according to the metric on the manifold. Then the density ratio at <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> compared with <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expressed as</p>
<table id="A5.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex207"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x)}{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x)}{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex207.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}(dy)-\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x_{i}}(dy)\bigg)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\bigg(\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x}(dy)-\int\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)k_{x_{i}}(dy)\bigg)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex208"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\exp\bigg(\int\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)\langle\nabla_{x}k_{x}(y)|_{x=\gamma_{t}},\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\rangle dydt\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mo>∫</mo></mrow></mstyle><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\exp\bigg(\int\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)\langle\nabla_{x}k_{x}(y)|_{x=\gamma_{t}},\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\rangle dydt\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We further control this using the Fisher information matrix,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex209" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}(x)=\int(\nabla_{x}\log k_{x}(y))(\nabla_{x}\log k_{x}(y))^{T}k_{x}(dy)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}(x)=\int(\nabla_{x}\log k_{x}(y))(\nabla_{x}\log k_{x}(y))^{T}k_{x}(dy),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and the quantity <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=\sup_{x\in{\mathcal{M}}}\sup_{v\in N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}}\frac{v^{T}\mathcal{I}(x)v}{\|v\|^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.0835em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=\sup_{x\in{\mathcal{M}}}\sup_{v\in N_{x}{\mathcal{M}}}\frac{v^{T}\mathcal{I}(x)v}{\|v\|^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. From the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we obtain the following bound:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex210"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\int\Big(\log" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>log</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\int\Big(\log</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex210.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)\langle\nabla_{x}k_{x}(y)|_{x=\gamma_{t}},\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\rangle dy" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)\langle\nabla_{x}k_{x}(y)|_{x=\gamma_{t}},\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\rangle dy</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex211"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\bigg(\int|\langle\nabla_{x}\log k_{x}(y)|_{x=\gamma_{t}},\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\rangle|^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}\bigg(\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\bigg(\int|\langle\nabla_{x}\log k_{x}(y)|_{x=\gamma_{t}},\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\rangle|^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}\bigg(\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex212"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\Big((\partial_{t}\gamma_{t})^{T}\mathcal{I}(x)(\partial_{t}\gamma_{t})\Big)^{1/2}\bigg(\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\Big((\partial_{t}\gamma_{t})^{T}\mathcal{I}(x)(\partial_{t}\gamma_{t})\Big)^{1/2}\bigg(\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex213"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq F^{1/2}\bigg(\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>F</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq F^{1/2}\bigg(\int\Big(\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big)^{2}k_{x}(dy)\bigg)^{1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Using the argument in the proof of Corollary <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem7" title="Corollary 3.7. ‣ 3.3 Log-domain smoothing and generalisation ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>, we can choose <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{0}\in[0,\tau/64]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{0}\in[0,\tau/64]</annotation></semantics></math> so that,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex214" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}\lesssim\max\{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}},\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo>≲</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\mu_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{2}+8\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}\varepsilon_{0}^{-d^{*}}\lesssim\max\{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}},\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Thus, borrowing the argument from (<a href="#A4.E39" title="Equation 39 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">39</span></a>) in the proof of Lemma <a href="#A4.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma D.4. ‣ D.2 Manifold concentration under log-domain smoothing ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>, we have that for all <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex215"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Big|\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Big|\log\hat{p}_{\epsilon}(y)+\frac{d}{2}\log(2\pi\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2})\Big|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex215.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+K)^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\max\{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}},\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}\}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≲</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>max</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></msubsup><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\lesssim\frac{(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+K)^{2}}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}+\max\{(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/d^{*}},\sigma_{\epsilon}^{\frac{4}{d^{*}+2}}c_{\mu}^{-\frac{2}{d^{*}+2}}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.6" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in{\mathcal{M}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in{\mathcal{M}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we also have the bound,</p>
<table id="A5.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex216"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+K)^{4}]^{1/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}_{Y\sim k_{x}}[(\operatorname{dist}(Y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})+K)^{4}]^{1/4}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex216.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}[(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{4}]^{1/4}+K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>dist</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>dist</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\mathbb{E}[(\operatorname{dist}(y,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})-\operatorname{dist}(x,{\mathcal{M}}^{\epsilon})^{4}]^{1/4}+K</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex217"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2K_{\max}^{1/2}K^{1/2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>K</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2K_{\max}^{1/2}K^{1/2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.7" class="ltx_p">In particular, there exists a quantity <math id="A5.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\lesssim 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>≲</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\lesssim 1</annotation></semantics></math>, such that the following bound on the density ratio holds:</p>
<table id="A5.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex218"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x)}{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x_{i})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>p</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x)}{\hat{p}^{k}_{\epsilon}(x_{i})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex218.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\exp\bigg(\frac{CF(KK_{\max}+(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/2d^{*}})}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt\bigg)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>C</mi><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>K</mi><mi>K</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>μ</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>d</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\exp\bigg(\frac{CF(KK_{\max}+(c_{\mu}^{2}N)^{-1/2d^{*}})}{\sigma_{\epsilon}^{2}}\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt\bigg).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, we must control the distance of the path <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>. We recall from the definition of <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\min}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\min}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A4.E44" title="Equation 44 ‣ Proof of Theorem . ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem ‣ Appendix D Proofs for the main results ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) and Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma C.7. ‣ C.3 Concentration under the manifold hypothesis ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.7</span></a>, that whenever <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq N_{\min}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq N_{\min}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</p>
<table id="A5.Ex219" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}\bigg(\inf_{x\in M}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\tau/2}(x))\geq c_{\mu}\frac{(\tau/2)^{d^{*}}}{4}\bigg)\geq 1-\delta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>data</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>μ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msup><mi>d</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msup><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}\bigg(\inf_{x\in M}\hat{\mu}_{\operatorname{data}}(B_{\tau/2}(x))\geq c_{\mu}\frac{(\tau/2)^{d^{*}}}{4}\bigg)\geq 1-\delta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">From this, it follows that with high probability, <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\inf_{i\in[N]}\|x-x_{i}\|\leq\tau/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>inf</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\inf_{i\in[N]}\|x-x_{i}\|\leq\tau/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Once we combine this with Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma C.4. ‣ C.2 Manifold reach ‣ Appendix C Lemmata ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.4</span></a>, we obtain the bound,</p>
<table id="A5.Ex220" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt\leq 2\|x-x_{i}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em">∂</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\int\|\partial_{t}\gamma_{t}\|dt\leq 2\|x-x_{i}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">completing the proof of the proposition.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experimental details</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide detailed descriptions of the experimental settings used in the paper.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>2-dimensional circle example</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The plots in <a href="#S3.F4" title="In 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> illustrate the trade-off that score-smoothing can provide for generalisation, to complement the theoretical results and discussion in <a href="#S3.SS3" title="3.3 Log-domain smoothing and generalisation ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>. We consider an empirical dataset of 12 uniformly spaced points on the unit circle, and generate samples using the smoothed score function with an isotropic Gaussian kernel. We use a variance exploding diffusion model with <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=9</annotation></semantics></math> and a geometric noise schedule, an Euler-Maruyama discretisation with 100 steps, and 1000 samples in the smoothing evaluation. In <a href="#S3.F4" title="In 3.2 The case of curved manifolds ‣ 3 Geometry-adaptivity of log-domain smoothing ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> we show how the resulting samples behave for different smoothing parameter <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>. Too little smoothing generates only training data, while too much smoothing causes generated samples to move towards the centre of the circle. There is a good choice of smoothing that balances between the two, promoting generalisation along the manifold (a phenomenon noticed by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib58" title="" class="ltx_ref">Scarvelis et al. [2025]</a></cite>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To further illustrate this trade-off, we also plot how the population negative log-likelihood changes as the degree of smoothing increases, averaged over 1000 points on the true circular manifold. We recall that one can calculate the log-likelihood of a point by integrating the divergence of the probability-flow ODE drift function along the probability flow ODE trajectory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2018</a>]</cite>. In our case, the drift of the probability flow ODE is a smoothed empirical score function.
As we are considering isotropic Gaussian smoothing, the divergence and the kernel convolution can be interchanged, allowing us to compute the log-likelihood by integrating the smoothed divergence of the empirical score function. The resulting plot exhibits a U-shape, clearly demonstrating the generalisation trade-off that arises from varying the smoothing level.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>Comparing Gaussian smoothing and KDE</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We here describe the experimental setup used in <a href="#S5.SS1" title="5.1 Generation in latent space ‣ 5 High-dimensional experiments ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">VAE</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We train the VAE on 10,000 samples from the MNIST database.
The VAE uses 16 initial feature channels, with scaling multiples of <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1,2,2,2)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1,2,2,2)</annotation></semantics></math> during downsampling, a convolutional kernel size of 3, a dropout rate of 0.1, and 4 groups for group normalisation. It maps into a 32-dimensional latent space. It is trained for 10,000 training steps with a batch size of 64, using the Adam optimiser <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">[<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kingma and Ba, 2015</a>]</cite> with learning rate 1e-3 and default parameters 0.9, 0.999.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Dataset construction</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use the remaining 60,000 points not used to train the VAE. The latent representations of the individual classes comprise lower-dimensional structures in the space, which we verify in <a href="#A6.F11" title="In Experiment hyperparameters ‣ F.2 Comparing Gaussian smoothing and KDE ‣ Appendix F Experimental details ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. To show this, for a particular class we map all points to the latent space. We then pick one of the latent points <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math>, and look at its 50 closest neighbours <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. We perform a PCA decomposition on the vectors <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z-z_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z-z_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to analyse their local structure. In <a href="#A6.F11" title="In Experiment hyperparameters ‣ F.2 Comparing Gaussian smoothing and KDE ‣ Appendix F Experimental details ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> we plot the cumulative explained variance, and observe that most of the variance is captured by fewer than the full 32 dimensions, suggesting that the latent representations for a particular class lie on a lower-dimensional manifold within the latent space.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We restrict to considering the digit 4, of which there are 5842 samples. We use these points to approximate the ‘true’ manifold <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}</annotation></semantics></math>, and randomly choose 100 points for use as the empirical dataset.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiment hyperparameters</h5>

<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a variance-exploding diffusion model with T = 9.0, a geometric noise schedule, and 100 generation steps with an Euler-Maruyama discretisation scheme. We generate 500 samples to calculate the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> distances reported in <a href="#S5.F7" title="In 5 High-dimensional experiments ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>. For the isotropic Gaussian kernel, we used smoothing with standard deviations <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\{0.04,0.05,0.06,0.07,0.08,0.09,0.1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.06</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.07</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.08</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.09</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\{0.04,0.05,0.06,0.07,0.08,0.09,0.1\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and we use 1000 smoothing samples at each generation step. For KDE, we use <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\{0.006,0.01,0.014,0.018,0.022,0.026\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.006</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.014</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.018</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.022</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.026</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\{0.006,0.01,0.014,0.018,0.022,0.026\}</annotation></semantics></math>, which were chosen to induce comparable average distances to the dataset from the generated samples (plotted along the <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>-axis).</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To obtain the samples plotted in <a href="#S5.F6" title="In 5 High-dimensional experiments ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, we use Gaussian-smoothing with standard deviations <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\{0.04,0.05,0.06,0.07\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.04</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.05</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.06</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.07</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\{0.04,0.05,0.06,0.07\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and KDE scales <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma\in\{0.015,0.03,0.045,0.06\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0.015</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.03</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.045</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0.06</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma\in\{0.015,0.03,0.045,0.06\}</annotation></semantics></math>. These were selected to induce comparable lateral distances along the manifold, computed as <math id="A6.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(d(x,\hat{\mu}_{data})^{2}-d(x,\mathcal{M})^{2})^{\frac{1}{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(d(x,\hat{\mu}_{data})^{2}-d(x,\mathcal{M})^{2})^{\frac{1}{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and averaged over 500 generated samples, which corresponds to inducing the same degree of ‘novelty’ relative to the training set. We display the same plot showing more samples in <a href="#A6.F12" title="In Experiment hyperparameters ‣ F.2 Comparing Gaussian smoothing and KDE ‣ Appendix F Experimental details ‣ Diffusion Models and the Manifold Hypothesis:Log-Domain Smoothing is Geometry Adaptive" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.F11" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A6.F11.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02305v1/mnist_pca_explained_variance_1s.svg" id="A6.F11.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/368;" width="476" height="368"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F11.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A6.F11.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Digit 1</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A6.F11.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02305v1/mnist_pca_explained_variance_4s.svg" id="A6.F11.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/368;" width="476" height="368"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F11.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A6.F11.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Digit 4</span></figcaption>
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_3">
<figure id="A6.F11.sf3" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02305v1/mnist_pca_explained_variance_5s.svg" id="A6.F11.sf3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/368;" width="476" height="368"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F11.sf3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(c)</span> </span><span id="A6.F11.sf3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Digit 5</span></figcaption>
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A6.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A6.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Verifying that latent representations of a digit class lie on a lower-dimensional structure in the latent space, by performing a PCA decomposition on the differences between nearby points.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
